diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..a9ebe68 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,36 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The shared layout exposes browser tools on every page in browsers with native
+[WebMCP support](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+The experimental API is feature-detected; ordinary controls also work without it.
+Both the current `document.modelContext` API and earlier
+`navigator.modelContext` previews are supported.
+
+| Tool | Inputs | Result / behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` (form) | `query` | Search titles and summaries; show matching articles and return metadata and links. |
+| `manage_reading_list` (form) | `action`: `view`, `add`, or `remove`; `slug` for mutations | Show and return the session reading list. |
+| `list_articles` | none | Return all article metadata and links. |
+| `get_article` | `slug` | Return metadata and article body as text, without executing article scripts. |
+| `open_article` | `slug` | Navigate to an existing article. |
+| `get_reading_list` | none | Return saved articles and links for the browser session. |
+| `set_article_saved` | `slug`, `saved` (boolean) | Save or remove an article and update visible bookmark controls. |
+
+The search and reading-list forms stay mounted when their flyouts are closed so
+agents can discover them. Agent activation opens the corresponding flyout; form
+submissions use native `FormData` and return results through `respondWith`.
+Tool names are unique across declarative forms and imperative registrations.
+Imperative tools are removed before Astro navigation and registered on page load.
+
+Reading-list changes use the existing session API. Explicit `add` and `remove`
+actions are idempotent; requests without an action retain the original toggle
+behavior. Unknown article slugs and invalid actions are rejected.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for Node-based tool, submission-helper, and API tests, or
+`pnpm run build` to compile the application. The tests use request and DOM stubs;
+they do not start a server or launch a browser.
